Caesar III game files go here
=============================

Julius needs the files of the original Caesar III, version 1.0.1.0 (the
GOG and Steam versions are; an older CD needs the 1.0.1.0 patch).

From an installed copy (GOG, Steam, or a Windows installation) copy
everything from the Caesar 3 folder into this folder, including the
555, smk and wavs folders.

From the CD: the files are in two places.
 - 555, SMK and wavs on the CD: copy these folders here (SMK as smk).
   Copy the CD's Soundfx files into wavs as well.
 - The other files are inside the installer archive data1.cab; unpack
   it on another computer (for instance with "unshield x data1.cab")
   and copy the files from its Exe folder here.

When it's right this folder holds, among others, c3.eng, c3_mm.eng,
C3.sg2, C3.555 and the folders 555, smk and wavs.

One file is called "North African" with a space. Copied from a PC, Mac,
network share or FAT card, RISC OS shows the space as a hard space;
that's the name Julius looks for.

Saved games and Julius's settings (julius.ini) are kept here too.
Or keep the files anywhere and *Set Julius$Data to that directory.
